# Runtime artifact dirs. Anchored to each known project root that produces them
# rather than a broad **/runtime/<sub>/ glob: an un-anchored glob would also match
# the tracked source/test trees app/runtime/ and tests/runtime/ and silently hide
# any future file added under e.g. tests/runtime/panel/ or app/runtime/settings/.
# Repo root:
/runtime/settings/
/runtime/builderops/
/runtime/dispatcher/
/runtime/orientation/
/runtime/panel/
/runtime/agent_memory/
/runtime/eval/
# companion-ui/companion-app (companion_ui tests run from this cwd and write
# runtime/panel/panel_confirmation.sqlite3 etc. relative to it):
/companion-ui/companion-app/runtime/settings/
/companion-ui/companion-app/runtime/builderops/
/companion-ui/companion-app/runtime/dispatcher/
/companion-ui/companion-app/runtime/orientation/
/companion-ui/companion-app/runtime/panel/
/companion-ui/companion-app/runtime/agent_memory/
# Promotion-plan receipts are local ops artifacts, not repo truth (#2081).
# Scoped to ops/promotions/ and ops/test-promotions/ only — tracked ops/** siblings (benchmarks, observability, quality) stay tracked.
ops/promotions/
ops/test-promotions/
verification_report.md

# Local hygiene artifacts
Archive/Trash/
tmp-dev/
tmp-test/
vault-test/
vaults/
tests/__init__.py
tests/orientation/__init__.py
tests/retrieval/__init__.py

# Local vault recovery artifacts
vault/Test fil1.md
vault/Workbench/Test fil 2.md
vault/System/companions/

# Dev DB snapshot dumps (dev-ergonomics / forensic; not for DR)
.db-snapshots/
